Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the sqlite3 module
=============================================

The native DBI driver belongs to qore-sqlite3-module.
HTML documentation and the upstream example test belong to the optional
qore-sqlite3-module-doc package. Debhelper creates matching debug symbols.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native build environment containing the packaged Qore runtime
and libqore-dev, then install the Build-Depends from debian/control. The current
qualification target is Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages.
Other Debian/Ubuntu releases and architectures need their own qualified SDK
and native build/test run. Cross builds are rejected because Qore executes
during the build. The system libsqlite3-dev package is required; no SQLite
implementation is bundled. No database server or credentials are required.

The build uses distribution compiler/hardening flags. Native Qore modules
resolve Qore symbols at load time without linking libqore. debian/rules derives
a minimum runtime and libqore SONAME package dependency from the installed SDK;
dh_shlibdeps supplies other shared-library dependencies. The runtime package is
not Multi-Arch: same because it requires the native Qore interpreter. There
are no AOT user modules or Qore dependency trailers in this module; ordinary
dh_strip is appropriate.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a fresh version for every changed upload. This snapshot precedes the 1.2.0
release. From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.2.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../sqlite3-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-sqlite3-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../sqlite3-package-work/qore-sqlite3-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../sqlite3-package-work/qore-sqlite3-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../sqlite3-package-work
    cp -a debian "../sqlite3-package-work/qore-sqlite3-module-$version/"
    cd "../sqlite3-package-work/qore-sqlite3-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc with dpkg-source -x into a clean directory. With dependencies
preinstalled, build as an unprivileged user with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Architecture-only builds (-B) do not need Doxygen; architecture-independent
builds (-A) produce documentation. Both DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc and
DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc suppress documentation; the profile also omits the doc
package. Do not use nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

The upstream suite runs against the newly built driver using a disposable
database file, including transactions, binary/NULL/large-integer values, regex
functions and sandbox checks. The PNG fixture is included with example tests.
Installed autopkgtests repeat the suite away from the build tree and compile
a fresh Qore program that loads sqlite3 and performs a database round trip.
This DBI-only module does not generate qpp metadata; compiler integration uses
the Datasource API provided by Qore. No optional Qore module is needed.

Check source/binary Lintian, detached debug symbols and hardening, installation
without libqore-dev, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall,
and reproducibility from two distinct build directories. Retain the exact source
commit, source/package hashes, dependency versions and logs. Publishing to the
testing PPA is separate from approval for a final general release.
